{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":25351850,"ns":0,"title":"Archival research","extract":"Archival research is a type of research which involves seeking out and extracting evidence from archival records. These records may be held either in collecting institutions, such as libraries and museums, or in the custody of the organization (whether a government body, business, family, or other agency) that originally generated or accumulated them, or in that of a successor body (transferring, or in-house archives).","description":"Type of research using evidence from archival records","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}